{"term":"collect","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0644bf4dfd4b03d0c6","definition":"To gather together; amass.","example":"Suzanne collected all the papers she had laid out.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["aggregate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:37f275d8ff503d7141","definition":"To get; particularly, get from someone.","example":"A bank collects a monthly payment on a client's new car loan. A mortgage company collects a monthly payment on a house.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["receive"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cc2605eaa9b3c1c49f","definition":"To accumulate (a number of similar or related objects), particularly for a hobby or recreation.","example":"John Henry collects stamps.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amound"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dc29b9bf1d152bafa4","definition":"To pick up or fetch","example":"Can you collect me from the airport?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["gather up","secure","gather","mass","merge","coalesce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:59174114f95ea9b1b4","definition":"To form a conclusion; to deduce, infer. (Compare gather, get.)","example":"[…] which consequence, I conceive, is very ill collected.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["gather up","secure","gather","mass","merge","coalesce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a5043637cecedddb75","definition":"To collect payments.","example":"He had a lot of trouble collecting on that bet he made.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["gather up","secure","gather","mass","merge","coalesce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:172d96e80718c41c05","definition":"To come together in a group or mass.","example":"The rain collected in puddles.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["group"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ddadb00c49c2c53b48","definition":"To infer; to conclude.","example":"Whence some collect that the former word imports a plurality of persons.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["assume","construe"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3b08bf6e9304daabeb","definition":"To collide with or crash into (another vehicle or obstacle).","example":"The truck veered across the central reservation and collected a car that was travelling in the opposite direction.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bump into","plough into","run into"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3f157734d1fc48991c","definition":"To be paid for by the recipient, as a telephone call or a shipment.","example":"It was to be a collect delivery, but no-one was available to pay.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0cedd2727830deb10d","definition":"With payment due from the recipient.","example":"I had to call collect.","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0dcb060e903d00482d","definition":"The prayer said before the reading of the epistle lesson, especially one found in a prayerbook, as with the Book of Common Prayer.","example":"He used the day's collect as the basis of his sermon.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"capitalized, sometimes","register":"capitalized, sometimes","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/kəˈlɛkt/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/